#!/usr/bin/env bash
# sweep_sqoop_rhs01_T8_s0
# DATASET: SQOOP rhs=1
# 20 runs, ~30 GPU-h (one seed of the 4x5 M x d plane at T=8).
# WHY: the M x d interaction. The medium's capacity argument predicts the d threshold
# moves with M (about d >= (M+1)/2); the axis sweeps at M=6 cannot show that.
# Split by task x T x seed: a lost box costs one seed of every cell, not every seed
# of some cells. Launch order: T=8 (the plane at the canonical T), then 4, 2, 16.
# Callbacks (from the sync_v16 bundle): accuracy, interventions, sync_metrics,
# t_variance (test-time T ramp) -- all log to the wandb summary at train end.
#     on vast: python scripts/vast/vast_run.py auto bash_scripts/sweep_sqoop_rhs01_T8_s0
